  "explanation": {
    "what_it_is": "NAC (N-acetylcysteine) is a modified form of the amino acid cysteine. It is readily absorbed and serves as a precursor to glutathione, one of the body's most important antioxidants and detoxification molecules.",
    "how_it_works": "NAC replenishes glutathione levels in cells, which neutralizes free radicals and supports the body's natural detoxification pathways. It also reduces inflammation by modulating immune signaling and improves mucus clearance in the lungs and gut. Additionally, NAC influences neurotransmitter balance\u2014particularly dopamine and serotonin\u2014which affects mood and stress resilience. By stabilizing blood sugar metabolism and supporting gut barrier function, it indirectly benefits multiple systems.",
